@smellophone 
HOW MUCH LONGER NOW...?

MY DELTARUNE.

@UncreativityMan That would genuinely be the most boring outcome possible, and Toby treating it like a big reveal that has to be hidden from the player would unironically be infantilizing. 

EVERY time a story sets up a mundane world like our own, and contrasts it with a fantastical world of adventure and escapism, the expected ending is that the worlds must separate to represent loss of childhood innocence and growing up. If you’re read a story before, you were expecting this to come up since chapter 1, especially considering the chapter is a microcosm this conflict with the Dark World being banished at the end. 

This would be like making the final prophecy, “the game would end eventually,” although at least that would be interesting as an in-universe meta-acknowledgement. Either way, it’s too predictable, too on-the-nose, and too cliche. Unless Toby is a complete hack, he’s clearly setting up an actual character death. That’s why Ralsei actually cares and would also pay off the obvious misdirect the game is deploying over the actual identity of “The Girl.”

@KiiBon Yes, I think the Darkners will be fine or maybe they can sadly exist in they way the exist with the Dark World. But I like to think they are fine just as in Undertale Flowey says: Hey, this guys are okay, don't worry, they are happy, you can now go foward... 
Before Chapter 5, I didnt think it could be this, but with Flowery, certainly. Maybe Ralsei is something else that can only exist when the Dark Worlds are open, maybe is because he feels sad about Susie house situation (even Kris in a way because they also did a room for Kris and Kris situation isn't much better either...) and try his best to help their friends. 
Susie could said that he wouldn't do that because of WHAT means so much for them...

